# ways — a mind that will not look at a way is not asked about it again
#
# A way on its line is asked for by itself: the mind chosen attends to that way or declines it, and
# has no other way to turn to. A declining hangs from the way's symbol, which stays where it was;
# the mind that declined is greyed in the popup for that way and for no other, and the next mind
# asked may not decline — a thing is declined once.
#
# --refuse-focus stands in for the choice judge answering "not this", which --playground never does.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Yard" --period dawn --refuse-focus

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180

# Childhood Memory is asked about the way to the field, and declines.
click observe "Test Field"
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
expect-state trees refusal way="the way to Test Field" mind=childhood_memory
expect-no-state trees element
expect-state noetic points=4/5
# The way is still to be looked at.
expect-state symbols click observe "the way to Test Field" in "Test Yard" (way)

# About that way it is not asked again...
click observe "Test Field"
expect-state popup childhood_memory(refused)
choose childhood_memory
expect-state noetic points=4/5

# ...and the mind asked after it attends: the way's one declining is spent.
choose comradeship
advance 12 180
expect-state trees element "the way to Test Field"
expect-state noetic points=3/5

# About another way, Childhood Memory may be asked.
click observe "Test Rock"
expect-state popup minds=[
expect-no-state popup (refused)
quit
